    {
      "pathPattern": "/api/discover",
      "method": "POST",
      "targetUrl": "pipeline",
      "stripPrefix": true,
      "order": 8,
      "timeout": 30000,
      "preserveHost": false,
      "forwardCookies": false,
      "proxyType": "pipeline",
      "isEnabled": true,
      "description": "Auto-discovery (#113): POST { url } -> http_request GET fetches the pasted site/feed URL server-side (dodging CORS, D12; failOnError:false so a common-path probe's 404 is data, not a halt) -> shape wraps the body in a JSON envelope { body, status, ok } (JSON.stringify escapes the HTML) -> respond. The browser DOMParses body for <link rel=alternate> feed links, or sniffs it as a feed. auth_required (allowApiKey).",
      "pipelineConfig": {
        "name": "Discover feed",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "fetch",
            "name": "fetch",
            "handlerType": "http_request",
            "config": {
              "url": "request.body.url",
              "method": "GET",
              "headers": {
                "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,application/rss+xml,application/atom+xml;q=0.8,*/*;q=0.7",
                "User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; Rivulet/1.0; +https://j5s.dev)"
              },
              "timeout": 20000,
              "failOnError": false
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "shape",
            "name": "shape",
            "handlerType": "function_handler",
            "config": {
              "code": "function handler({ steps }) {\n  var f = (steps && steps.fetch) || {}\n  var raw = f.body\n  var body = (typeof raw === 'string') ? raw : (raw == null ? '' : JSON.stringify(raw))\n  return {\n    json: JSON.stringify({\n      body: body,\n      status: (typeof f.status === 'number') ? f.status : 0,\n      ok: (f.ok === true)\n    })\n  }\n}\n"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "respond",
            "name": "respond",
            "handlerType": "response_handler",
            "config": {
              "body": "{{{steps.shape.json}}}",
              "status": 200,
              "headers": { "Cache-Control": "no-store" },
              "contentType": "application/json"
            }
          }
        ],
        "validators": [{ "type": "auth_required", "config": { "allowApiKey": true } }]
      }
    },
    {
      "pathPattern": "/api/prune",
      "method": "POST",
      "targetUrl": "pipeline",
      "stripPrefix": true,
      "order": 9,
      "timeout": 30000,
      "preserveHost": false,
      "forwardCookies": false,
      "proxyType": "pipeline",
      "isEnabled": true,
      "description": "Retention (#119): cutoff = now - 30d (epoch ms) -> data_delete(reader_items) delete-by-query where read=true AND starred!=true AND fetchedAt < cutoff -> respond { pruned: count }. Starred/unread rows never match (exempt by construction). Fired nightly by a pipeline_schedule as system context. No auth_required validator: the reader alias is private (edge-gated), so this is protected at the site level, and the CE scheduler runs it with NO user — auth_required would reject a userless system run.",
      "pipelineConfig": {
        "name": "Prune old items (retention)",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "cutoff",
            "name": "cutoff",
            "handlerType": "function_handler",
            "config": {
              "code": "function handler() {\n  var THIRTY_DAYS_MS = 2592000000\n  return { ms: Date.now() - THIRTY_DAYS_MS }\n}\n"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "del",
            "name": "del",
            "handlerType": "data_delete",
            "config": {
              "filters": {
                "read": { "op": "eq", "value": "true" },
                "starred": { "op": "ne", "value": "true" },
                "fetchedAt": { "op": "lt", "value": "steps.cutoff.ms" }
              },
              "schemaId": "96a1b5e7-96f0-43a4-baa8-2e19b539d07c",
              "filterLogic": "and"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "respond",
            "name": "respond",
            "handlerType": "response_handler",
            "config": {
              "body": "{\"pruned\":{{steps.del.count}}}",
              "status": 200,
              "headers": { "Cache-Control": "no-store" },
              "contentType": "application/json"
            }
          }
        ],
        "validators": []
      }
    },
    {
      "pathPattern": "/api/feeds/folder",
      "method": "POST",
      "targetUrl": "pipeline",
      "stripPrefix": true,
      "order": 10,
      "timeout": 30000,
      "preserveHost": false,
      "forwardCookies": false,
      "proxyType": "pipeline",
      "isEnabled": true,
      "description": "Move a feed between folders: POST { url, folder } -> prep coerces url + normalizes folder (empty -> null) -> query finds the reader_feeds row by url -> pick recordId -> data_update writes { folder } only (conditional) -> respond { ok, updated }. The add endpoint's data_upsert_many is insert-only (ce#407) so it can't change an existing feed's folder; this is the update twin, mirroring /api/items/read. auth_required (allowApiKey). bffless/apps#133.",
      "pipelineConfig": {
        "name": "Set feed folder",
        "steps": [
          {
            "id": "prep",
            "name": "prep",
            "handlerType": "function_handler",
            "config": {
              "code": "function handler({ request }) {\n  var b = (request && request.body) || {}\n  var url = (typeof b.url === 'string') ? b.url.trim() : ''\n  var folder = (b.folder != null && typeof b.folder === 'string' && b.folder.trim() !== '') ? b.folder.trim() : null\n  return {\n    url: url,\n    folder: folder,\n    hasUrl: !!url,\n    noUrl: !url\n  }\n}\n"
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "query",
            "name": "query",
            "handlerType": "data_query",
            "config": {
              "filters": { "url": { "op": "eq", "value": "steps.prep.url" } },
              "pageSize": 1,
              "schemaId": "d1216df3-9776-4de2-81b0-0343d758f83d",
              "condition": "steps.prep.hasUrl"
            }
          },
